# image-handle members named and refused by the GRAMMAR, rather than
# half-supported (#2794)
#
# BOTH DIRECTIONS ARE HERE. `albedo` below is a `sampler2d` bound exactly as
# `spirv-sampled-image` binds it, and it draws no diagnostic; every declaration
# after it differs from a compiling one in ONE property, and each draws a sentence
# naming that property. Without the compiling binding at the top, a case that
# rejected every handle spelling outright would pass this just as well.
#
# THE GRAMMAR HALF ONLY. Reading a spelling and refusing a member of it happens
# during name resolution, and a module with a resolution error never reaches the
# checks that decide whether a handle is bound correctly - so those live in
# `spirv-sampler-binding-refused` and cannot share a build with these.

# COMPILES. the control: the same declaration the sampled-image case emits, in a
# file the harness expects to fail, so a rule that refused handles generally would
# add a line to the golden here.
#[sampler(0, 0)] var albedo: sampler2d;

# REFUSED: depth comparison, which #2794 puts out of scope by name. It differs from
# `albedo` in the `shadow` suffix and nothing else.
#[sampler(0, 1)] var shadow_map: sampler2dshadow;

# REFUSED: multisampled, which is fetched per sample rather than sampled at all.
#[sampler(0, 2)] var msaa: sampler2dms;

# REFUSED: the dimensionalities that need a further capability and a different
# sampling path. Each is read as itself, so the message names the dimensionality.
#[sampler(0, 3)] var screen: samplerrect;
#[sampler(0, 4)] var texels: samplerbuffer;

# REFUSED: a storage image, which is read and written directly rather than sampled.
# It is refused as a FORM rather than by dimensionality: no dimensionality of it is
# emitted, so a message naming `2d` would invite a reader to try `3d`.
#[sampler(0, 5)] var target: image2d;

# REFUSED: a declaration whose name the handle grammar claims. The spelling
# resolves in type position ahead of scope, so the record would be unreachable -
# and this holds for a REFUSED spelling too, since whether a member is emitted yet
# must not decide whether a declaration is legal.
rec sampler3d {
    x: f32;
}

fun main() i32 {
    ret 0;
}
